<title>JAPAN: Shintom to absorb subsidiary in October.</title>
<headline>Shintom to absorb subsidiary in October.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shintom Co Ltd said on Thursday that it would absorb its wholly owned subsidiary Kofu Housei KK on October 1 through a merger.</p>
<p>Shintom makes electronic equipment and electric parts for vehicles. Kofu Housei assembles electronic equipment.</p>
<p>In the merger transaction, 25.8 shares of Kofu Housei will be exchanged for one Shintom share.</p>
<p>Shintom has forecast that its parent sales will total 53.26 billion yen and that its parent current profit will reach 2.15 billion yen in the year to March 1998.</p>
</text>
